  "description": "KADCAX crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C43 H43 Cl3 N6 O11 Tb3 1+,C45 H47 Cl3 N6 O11 Tb3 1+,H2 O1,2(Cl1 1-). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 3 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.586-3.593 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.16-98.01°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C88H92Cl8N12O23Tb6.",
